---
/**
 * Hero illustration: the blog's own tags as a word cloud.
 *
 * From the Claude Design project "Illustrations hero banner Zatsit", board 3a.
 * The design's own reasoning: the seventeen tags that actually exist on the
 * blog, ranked by weight rather than laid out at random, so the figure says
 * what the blog talks about instead of decorating the space. Poppins only, no
 * rotated words.
 *
 * Three things changed on the way in, all measured rather than preferred.
 *
 * The design set `green` and `environnement` in `--color-eco`. That token is a
 * signifier for fills and shapes and measures 2.01:1 on this band in the light
 * theme, so those two words failed WCAG at any size. They now use
 * `--color-eco-text`, added for this: the same hue and saturation taken down to
 * 30% lightness, 4.93:1 on the light surface, unchanged in the dark theme where
 * the bright green already measured 7.19:1.
 *
 * The quiet group carried `fill-opacity: 0.65`, which put it at 3.14:1 in light
 * and 3.33:1 in dark against a 4.5:1 requirement. The opacity is gone; size and
 * weight carry the hierarchy, which is enough for a word cloud.
 *
 * And the weights are 400, 600 and 700 rather than the design's 500, because
 * those are the three the site actually downloads. Asking for 500 would have
 * had the browser synthesise it from another file.
 *
 * `role="img"` with a label listing the tags: seventeen words read out one by
 * one would be noise, and none of them is a link.
 */
---

<svg
  class="tagcloud"
  viewBox="0 0 600 460"
  role="img"
  aria-label="Nuage de mots des thèmes du blog : architecture, cloud, IA, data, green, environnement, dev, web, open-source, java, tech, javascript, hacktoberfest, conference, refacto, frontend, général."
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
>
  <defs>
    <radialGradient id="tagcloud-glow" cx="0.5" cy="0.5" r="0.5">
      <stop offset="0" stop-color="currentColor" stop-opacity="0.16"></stop>
      <stop offset="1" stop-color="currentColor" stop-opacity="0"></stop>
    </radialGradient>
  </defs>

  <g class="tagcloud__glow">
    <ellipse cx="300" cy="230" rx="280" ry="190" fill="url(#tagcloud-glow)"></ellipse>
  </g>

  <g class="tagcloud__words" text-anchor="middle">
    {/* The four domains the blog leads with. */}
    <g class="tagcloud__major">
      <text x="320" y="142" font-size="40">architecture</text>
      <text x="250" y="212" font-size="36">cloud</text>
      <text x="400" y="204" font-size="30">ai</text>
      <text x="300" y="347" font-size="32">data</text>
    </g>

    {/* Sustainability keeps its own colour: it is the one subject where this
        blog claims something checkable. */}
    <g class="tagcloud__eco">
      <text x="440" y="280" font-size="34">green</text>
      <text x="400" y="80" font-size="20">environnement</text>
    </g>

    <g class="tagcloud__minor">
      <text x="120" y="140" font-size="24">dev</text>
      <text x="510" y="140" font-size="24">web</text>
      <text x="270" y="278" font-size="28">open-source</text>
      <text x="110" y="208" font-size="22">java</text>
      <text x="460" y="342" font-size="24">tech</text>
      <text x="400" y="402" font-size="22">javascript</text>
    </g>

    <g class="tagcloud__quiet">
      <text x="160" y="80" font-size="16">hacktoberfest</text>
      <text x="510" y="208" font-size="16">conference</text>
      <text x="110" y="275" font-size="18">refacto</text>
      <text x="130" y="342" font-size="20">frontend</text>
      <text x="240" y="402" font-size="18">general</text>
    </g>
  </g>

  <g class="tagcloud__dots">
    <circle cx="80" cy="110" r="3" fill-opacity="0.4"></circle>
    <circle cx="530" cy="90" r="3" fill-opacity="0.4"></circle>
    <circle cx="70" cy="380" r="3" fill-opacity="0.4"></circle>
    <circle cx="540" cy="390" r="3" fill-opacity="0.4"></circle>
    <circle cx="300" cy="55" r="3" fill-opacity="0.3"></circle>
  </g>
</svg>

<style>
  .tagcloud {
    inline-size: min(30rem, 46%);
    block-size: auto;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    /* The glow is drawn past the viewBox and would be clipped otherwise. */
    overflow: visible;
  }

  .tagcloud__words text {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }

  /* currentColor on the group, so each block declares its colour once and both
     the fill and the gradient stops follow the theme. */
  .tagcloud__glow,
  .tagcloud__dots {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    fill: currentColor;
  }

  .tagcloud__major {
    fill: var(--color-primary);
    font-weight: var(--font-bold);
  }

  .tagcloud__eco {
    fill: var(--color-eco-text);
    font-weight: var(--font-bold);
  }

  .tagcloud__eco text:last-child {
    font-weight: var(--font-semibold);
  }

  .tagcloud__minor {
    fill: var(--color-text);
    fill-opacity: 0.75;
    font-weight: var(--font-semibold);
  }

  .tagcloud__quiet {
    fill: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-weight: var(--font-regular);
  }

  /* Below the breakpoint where the hero stacks, the figure would push the
     actions off the first screen. It says nothing the page does not say
     elsewhere: /tags/ lists the same seventeen, as links. */
  @media (max-width: 899px) {
    .tagcloud {
      display: none;
    }
  }
</style>
